-- STRICT EQUALITY OPERATOR ------------------------------------- main.kl  K0901

Kalam has no `===` or `!==`. Its `==` and `!=` are already strict: values of different types are never silently converted before comparing.

4│     else if n === 0:
                 ^^^

Try: `==`

Help: Write `==` instead of `===`, and `!=` instead of `!==`. `kalam fix` does this for you.

Learn more: kalam explain K0901
